    <sys:String x:Key="S.Wizard.WelcomeTitle">Welcome</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Wizard.WelcomeText">WebcamFBT tracks your body from your webcam and sends it to SteamVR as virtual trackers, so you get full body tracking in VRChat, Vivecraft and other SteamVR games without buying trackers.&#x0a;&#x0a;Supported headsets: Meta Quest 1, 2, 3, 3S and Pro (Link cable, Air Link, Steam Link, Virtual Desktop or ALVR), Oculus Rift and Rift S, and other headsets that work with SteamVR (Valve Index, HTC Vive, Pico, Windows Mixed Reality).&#x0a;&#x0a;This wizard gets everything ready in a few steps. You can open it again any time from the General section.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Wizard.DriverTitle">SteamVR driver</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Wizard.DriverText">For the trackers to show up in SteamVR, the WebcamFBT driver must be installed. If it is not, close SteamVR and press the button below.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Wizard.CameraTitle">Camera</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Wizard.CameraText">Pick the camera to use. Virtual cameras (OBS, Meta Quest Link) don't show the room, so don't pick those. Scan opens the real cameras to check that they work. You can add extra cameras later under Camera and model.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Wizard.NoCameras">No camera found. Is the webcam plugged in? Is Windows camera access on (Settings &gt; Privacy &amp; security &gt; Camera)?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Wizard.VirtualNote">Entries marked 'virtual' were added by OBS or the Meta Quest software; they won't show you.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Wizard.PlacementTitle">Place the camera</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Wizard.PlacementText">• Put the camera in front of the play area, about 2–3 m away.&#x0a;• At waist height (~1 m off the floor), looking straight ahead.&#x0a;• Your whole body must be visible head to toe, feet included.&#x0a;• Keep the room well lit; in the dark the camera slows down.&#x0a;&#x0a;If unsure, once the engine runs, the Setup assistant under Camera and model shows on a map where to put the camera, or scores the spot you picked.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Wizard.CalibrationTitle">Calibration and games</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="S.Wizard.CalibrationText">1. Start the engine, connect your headset to the PC and start SteamVR.&#x0a;2. Wearing the headset, stand in front of the camera, look ahead and hold still for 2 seconds. It calibrates by itself: two short beeps, then a high beep when done. Shoulders to feet must be in view; the head may be out of the picture.&#x0a;3. Run your game's full body calibration:&#x0a;   • VRChat: T-pose, then pull both triggers.&#x0a;   • Vivecraft: set the model type to Split Arms/Legs in Playermodel Settings, then Calibrate FBT.&#x0a;&#x0a;To recalibrate (after recentering the headset or moving the camera) hold both hands above your head for 2 seconds, or press {0}.</sys:String>
